# the instruction-level builder: encodes into sections of a mink object, with labels, relaxation, relocations and its statement record
#
# a builder holds the sections of one object over one registered set and a
# selection. each section is a list of fragments, an instruction, data bytes,
# a zero fill or an alignment, and its cursor is its end, so switching keeps
# every section's place. labels are the handles a symbolic operand names, and
# a label is local until it is exposed with a binding, a visibility and a kind.
#
# `finish` lays the sections out to a fixed point, encodes every fragment and
# hands back mink's neutral object. a fixup of any step of an instruction's
# form, grown or not, folds into its bytes when its operand is relative or a
# pc-relative address, its target is a label of the same section that cannot
# be preempted, its relocation kind is plain pc-relative, and no instruction
# the linker may resize lies between. every other fixup becomes a relocation
# through the set's bindings. an instruction grows by the set's relaxation
# rows when its target is out of range, measured by the layout whether or not
# the fixup folds, or when only the linker knows the target, as llvm-mc grows
# a branch to an undefined symbol. growth is the only change a pass makes to
# an instruction, and every length is the length of an encoding, never a sum
# of field widths.
#
# an instruction is written in the shortest form the set's compressions and
# the selection admit when it is emitted, once, and relaxation then grows
# that form, so a compressed branch relaxes through the set's rows like any
# other. a branch or jump to a label is written compressed when the set
# relaxes the compressed row on that operand, so the layout starts it at its
# shortest form and grows it to the shortest that reaches: `beq a0, zero, l`
# is c.beqz while l is in reach and beq or the inverted branch past a jal
# when it is not. the steps of a longer form that do not take the target are
# written in their shortest form, as llvm-mc writes c.bnez past the jal.
#
# the layout ends within a stated bound of passes. it starts every
# instruction at its shortest form and only ever grows one, so a pass that
# does not end grows at least one instruction by one relaxation, and an
# instruction grows at most as many times as its row's chain of relaxations
# is long (`relax.depth`), which the set's check bounds. with n instructions
# of chains d1..dn, the layout takes at most 1 + d1 + ... + dn passes, and a
# layout that has not settled by then, which only a set whose lengths depend
# on their values could make, is refused rather than run on.
#
# a datum, a symbol's address or distance as data, folds or relocates
# by the rule an instruction's fixup does. code alignment after an
# instruction the linker may resize pads its worst case and carries the set's
# realign marker, so the linker can shrink it back. a fixup whose relocation
# covers instructions after its own, as a call pair's, is written only in a
# sequence that holds them, with the marker the set's span states beside it.
#
# every fragment is written under a context, the object's or another the
# caller states over the same register file, narrower as a source dialect's
# `.option norvc` keeps instructions full length or wider as `.option arch,
# +zbb` admits what the object's selection lacks. its admission, its encoding,
# its shortest form, its relaxation and its code fill are that context's. what
# the object states as a whole is the object's: its architecture is entered by
# the object's context, its selection traits are the object's selection's, and
# a derived trait holds when the object's context or any context written under
# admits it. a convention trait is the caller's abi row's, a fixed one the
# architecture row's, and a source trait the source's or the set's default.
#
# a frame and a constant-time range are handed to mink as typed records:
# `cfi_start`, `cfi` and `cfi_end` state a function's frame by rules at the
# statements they precede, starting from the frame the set states for the
# architecture, and `ct_begin` and `ct_end` mark a range mink's object keeps
# in memory. masc writes no frame bytes, mink owns them.
#
# the surface a consumer builds against is frozen: `make`, `traits`, `open`,
# `switch`, `label`, `define`, `expose`, `align`, `data`, `datum`, `finish`,
# `Size`, the typed `Refusal`, `cfi` with its frame calls and `ct_begin` and
# `ct_end`. it grows by new calls, never by changing these. masc owns every
# byte count after relaxation, so a consumer reads `Size`, the layout and the
# listing and never restates one.
#
# nothing here names an architecture or a format: the fill, the relaxations,
# the compressions, the bindings and the markers are the set's, and sections,
# symbols and relocations are mink's neutral rows.

